A||||6||LT1 Chop Top||How do you remove a GT steering wheel??||||5||
Z||000000||LT1 Chop Top||08-20-2001||07:11 PM||||How do you remove a GT (3-spoke) steering wheel?? Just want to know before I get started and mess something up!!<P>I accidentally posted this Q in the General section too......whoop.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||LT1 Chop Top||08-20-2001||07:12 PM||||BTW, what is a steering wheel puller for??<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-20-2001||07:22 PM||||the shaft and the steering wheel are both tapered and they are pressed together.thats what you need the puller for I think you can rent one from auto zone for a couple bucks ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||08-20-2001||07:56 PM||||My kids got the one off our parts car without a puller, and did it rather quickly too.  I'll ask em how, and try to get you an answer if some-1 doesn't beat me to it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||lawrence||08-20-2001||08:30 PM||||Actually, you don't need a puller for this steering wheel, you need a "pusher".<P>When you push the wheel toward the dash, it relieves the pressure on a snap ring.  You then pull the snap ring off and the wheel comes right off.<P>Be careful because the horn wire is there and you don't want to pull it off.  Also, the wheel is being pushed by a spring, so when you pull the wheel off the spines, make sure it doesn't hit you in the face!<P>And don't forget to mark the spines so you put the wheel back where it was.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/products" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/products</A>  - WebElectric Products||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||08-21-2001||05:21 AM||||Use the puller to remove the wheel. Lawrence is refering to the locking ring tool that you use if you are going furthur into the column.<BR>the end of the shaft and the wheel hub are already marked for position.||||reg||1
Z||000006||gabriel||08-22-2001||12:29 PM||||Greetings:<P> The tool to remove the plate is a "lock plate depresser" and I don't have a clue how you could remove the plate without one.  You can buy them most anywhere. -Even Sears stocks them.<P> &gt;so when you pull the wheel off the spines, make sure it doesn't hit you in the face!<P>  The lock plate itself flew off and hit me right in the mouth once  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> so take care.  You still need the puller to remove the wheel.<BR>             -g||||reg||1
